1
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,877
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,972
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:27,707
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,657
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,597
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,000
Believe in wonder.

17
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:21,097
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't wanna live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,657
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:42,800
We live in wonderland.

26
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:00,620
Our nightmares aren't
over, Princess. Not yet.

27
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:01,681
The man's right!

28
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:02,650
Yeah!

29
00:02:02,733 --> 00:02:04,717
I wish what happened was a
nightmare, but it was real!

30
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:05,741
We want justice!

31
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:08,597
We saw King Cobra attack
Nanohana with our own eyes!

32
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,510
That's right!

33
00:02:09,593 --> 00:02:11,496
And those damn royals shot Koza, too!

34
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,577
You expect us all just to forgive
them after what they did?!

35
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:20,307
Our nightmares will only be over once
we've killed every royal in this country!

36
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:26,640
Royal Army, drop your weapons now!

37
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:32,520
Up there!

38
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:35,460
Chaka!

39
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,120
Is he serious?

40
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:39,700
Yes!

41
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:43,200
Ma! Ma! Ma!

42
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:46,380
That goes for you too, Rebel Army.

43
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:51,180
Igaram!

44
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:52,340
Squad captain!

45
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:08,660
He made it back.

46
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:16,052
May we meet again safely in
our homeland, Princess Phoebe.

47
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,917
Hey, it's that cross-dressing
guy from Whiskey Peak.

48
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,177
He's still alive.

49
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:25,760
Hey, who is that guy?

50
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,660
Boy, can you talk to me?

51
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,980
That's the boy from Nanohana.

52
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,937
The kid who was harmed by
those royal army goons.

53
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:38,057
No, that's not true!

54
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:38,970
It wasn't them!

55
00:03:39,053 --> 00:03:41,497
The people who did this looked
like members of the royal army,

56
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:42,777
but it really wasn't them!

57
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:44,157
Everyone, please listen!

58
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,358
This is what I saw!

59
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:48,830
Ooh!

60
00:03:48,913 --> 00:03:50,940
It feels so good to get back into gear!

61
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:01,850
That's right.

62
00:04:01,933 --> 00:04:03,197
We were all manipulated.

63
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:05,751
This battle was a plot from the beginning.

64
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,760
Yakuza, leader...

65
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:13,697
Royal or rebel, I'll
explain it to you all.

66
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:16,486
Everything that has
befallen our fair country.

67
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:19,500
But only if you drop your weapons.

68
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:35,230
Princess?

69
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:41,200
My friends, where are they?

70
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,824
Come on, Usopp, I know
you're hurt, but keep up.

71
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:49,537
I wish I could, but I'm coming down with,
if I walk anymore, I'll die disease.

72
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:51,140
I'll drag you then. Wait,

73
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:56,027
let me go, or I can come down with, if
I get dragged anymore, I'll die disease.

74
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:57,150
Found him.

75
00:05:01,980 --> 00:05:05,797
Who are you uh just
travelers passing through

76
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:07,777
the guy on your back's one of us as well!

77
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:10,537
We'll take him now thanks old man!

78
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:13,797
Hold on if you're with this
young man then you must

79
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:16,317
be those Pirates who brought
Vivi back to this country?

80
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:20,820
Wait how would you know all
that daddy everyone? Everyone!

81
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:23,900
Hey, Phoebe!

82
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:25,850
Daddy?

83
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:28,550
What?!

84
00:05:28,633 --> 00:05:30,017
This guy is Phoebe's dad?!

85
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,865
Guess that makes you the king.

86
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:32,990
Yes,

87
00:05:33,073 --> 00:05:34,457
and I'd be a dead king if it weren't for

88
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:37,128
the efforts of your
brave young friend here.

89
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:40,697
Even though he'd come into contact
with Crocodile's poison hook,

90
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:44,020
I still managed to carry
myself and another to safety.

91
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:46,640
An unbelievable strength he has.

92
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:49,377
Should we be worried about the poison?

93
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:51,337
I mean, is he going to be all right?

94
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:52,250
It's okay.

95
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:54,262
It should be neutralized by now.

96
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:57,397
However, his injuries need to be treated.

97
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:58,760
So do yours as well.

98
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,630
We'll wait.

99
00:06:02,713 --> 00:06:04,385
You need to be somewhere else.

100
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:06,287
Go back to the square, Vivi.

101
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:07,990
He's right.

102
00:06:08,073 --> 00:06:09,257
Now that the war's over,

103
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:12,497
it's only fitting for the king and princess
to say a few words, don't you think?

104
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,617
You know, tell them what really happened.

105
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:17,700
Right, and I can tell them
all about you guys, too.

106
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:19,760
Vivi, dear, please don't.

107
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:23,600
We're a band of notorious pirates.

108
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:27,277
The last thing we need are
our faces and names known.

109
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:29,260
But what we do need is food.

110
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:30,660
And rest.

111
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:33,642
We'd like to crash at the
palace, if that's okay.

112
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,020
Yes, sir.

113
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:56,268
Understood, Captain Smoker.

114
00:06:57,260 --> 00:06:58,460
Are you serious?

115
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:00,490
Crocodile?

116
00:07:00,573 --> 00:07:02,340
He was the one behind all this?

117
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,953
All this time, we thought he was a hero.

118
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:07,540
Over there! Look!

119
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,000
It's the Marines!

120
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:18,377
I've just been informed that a
Baroque Works ship has been seized,

121
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:21,401
one that makes artificial
rain using dance powder.

122
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:26,037
You being Baroque Works president,
I've been ordered to tell you this.

123
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:29,179
Sir Crocodile, one of the
Seven Warlords of the Sea.

124
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:33,980
Tell me!

125
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:36,141
Tell me which way Crocodile went!

126
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:41,257
By the authority of the world government,

127
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:44,417
I hereby strip you of your
authorization to capture enemy ships,

128
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:48,017
as well as all the titles and rights
bestowed upon you by the government.

129
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:51,865
Additionally, you and all Baroque
Works agents are under arrest.

130
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:14,240
Oh, that's my cue to leave.

131
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:26,340
We rebels, we've done horrible
things that could never be undone.

132
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:31,820
Leader, I don't know what to
say to him, to any of them.

133
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:37,820
We all feel regret over what has
happened, but that's natural.

134
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:42,440
King Cobra, your majesty.

135
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:45,300
We've lost so much and gained nothing.

136
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:46,860
We've been divided.

137
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:53,224
But now we have a chance
to take a step forward.

138
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:56,877
No matter who you fought against,
the battle did occur and it's over.

139
00:08:56,960 --> 00:09:00,195
We must put this strife behind
us and become one again.

140
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:04,420
The king's right.

141
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:08,157
Unfortunately, there's nothing
we can do about what's happened.

142
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,780
We cannot change the past.

143
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:17,685
There's one thing we can change,
however, and that's our future.

144
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,420
He's so wise.

145
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:35,860
A future where all of
Alabasta is united once more.

146
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:43,120
The monumental battle that will be
engraved upon the annals of history...

147
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:59,240
...and even more importantly, the
battle that will never be told...

148
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:05,360
...is finally over.

149
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:12,284
Smoker, where the hell
is this rain coming from?

150
00:10:12,540 --> 00:10:15,658
Don't tell me you used the
dance powder on this ship.

151
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:17,480
Don't be stupid.

152
00:10:18,540 --> 00:10:21,717
Believe it or not, I know
better than to commit a crime.

153
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:23,877
We haven't seen each
other in quite some time,

154
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:26,957
and the first thing you do is
blame me for some natural rain.

155
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:29,511
And I was about to tell you you look good.

156
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:30,670
You're right.

157
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,300
It was a lousy welcome. Hina's sorry.

158
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:35,154
As for the compliment,

159
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:38,157
I can't believe the white hunter
would say something so sweet.

160
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,980
My, you've actually softened up a little.

161
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:42,860
Shut your trap, Hina.

162
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:45,557
Is that what I get for helping you out?

163
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:48,097
And I might add, for
the umpteenth time, too?

164
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:50,237
My elite unit found this ship for you.

165
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,673
A thanks would be nice.

166
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:53,650
Upset.

167
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:54,600
Hina's upset.

168
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:56,597
Oh, don't give me that speech.

169
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:58,780
We're all marines. Oh, honestly.

170
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:02,275
I don't know how poor Tashigi
puts up with you, Smoker.

171
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:05,060
She manages somehow.

172
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:09,600
I need you to take this ship into HQ me.

173
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:13,037
Also Toshiki is going to
be bringing crocodile here

174
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:15,937
kill two birds with one
stone and take him with you?

175
00:11:16,020 --> 00:11:17,000
Give me a break.

176
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:19,788
I'm an officer not your
personal errand girl

177
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:24,700
It's heads.

178
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:29,560
It's tails you lose, errand girl?

179
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:32,257
You're a real piece of work.

180
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:33,477
You know that smoker

181
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:36,817
I thought a few years of command would
change you, but I guess I was wrong.

182
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:38,076
Hina's disappointed.

183
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:39,853
I'm well aware of that.

184
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,420
And I don't care.

185
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:48,410
Negative.

186
00:11:48,493 --> 00:11:49,323
That's an order.

187
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:50,422
Sergeant Major!

188
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:52,340
With all due respect, why not?

189
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:56,397
With your permission, we can capture
all the Straw Hats in one fell swoop!

190
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:57,310
Denied!

191
00:11:57,393 --> 00:11:59,657
I will not allow you to
lay a hand on any of them!

192
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:00,570
Is that understood?

193
00:12:00,653 --> 00:12:03,897
But we're never going to get
another chance like this again.

194
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:05,862
They're sitting ducks right now.

195
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:09,080
Hang on, Leader.

196
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:11,067
We'll get you taken care of.

197
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:14,040
And your father, too.

198
00:12:14,380 --> 00:12:17,120
Leader, there was a sandstorm in Yuba.

199
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:19,700
Still a war reward, as always, I see.

200
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:24,197
I don't know how Yuba fared,
but take my word for it,

201
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:27,104
a sandstorm is no match
for my stubborn old man.

202
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,380
I hope so.

203
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,187
Don't worry about me either.

204
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,264
I've got his blood in my veins.

205
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:36,620
As soon as I get treated,
I'll head to Yuba.

206
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:39,057
I'll keep you updated.

207
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:40,552
So don't worry, alright?

208
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:41,530
Alright.

209
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,620
It's actually raining!

210
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,097
This is the first time in three years!

211
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:48,010
It's a miracle!

212
00:12:48,093 --> 00:12:50,021
This rain will end the rebellion!

213
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:52,140
Our foolish sons will come home!

214
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:12,785
How long are you going
to be stubborn, old man?

215
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,536
Father, look around.

216
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:15,720
Yuba is finished.

217
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:16,880
A ghost town.

218
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:19,437
What are you going to do here by yourself?

219
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:21,638
Are you going to dry up and die too?

220
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:22,730
Old man!

221
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,180
See, son.

222
00:13:27,740 --> 00:13:29,177
Look there!

223
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:31,100
The rain has come back.

224
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:38,280
Just like I told you, I knew
that it would come back.

225
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:44,417
I was right. Yes.

226
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:46,160
Right as rain.

227
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:53,697
The rain that falls in the kingdom
is more than just a physical one,

228
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:59,880
but also a symbolic one that washes away
the bitter tears of its recent past.

229
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:18,460
Princess Vivi, what
are you still doing up?

230
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:21,500
Oh, hey, Couran, it's nothing.

231
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:25,560
You can't sleep, huh?

232
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,260
It's not that.

233
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:30,536
I just don't want to sleep right now.

234
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:33,304
I'd rather watch the rain fall.

235
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:36,100
It's been so long since I've seen it.

236
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:54,140
Bebe, about Pell.

237
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:58,280
He was, without a doubt, the strongest,

238
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:01,619
most loyal and dignified
warrior I ever served with.

239
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:03,357
He was.

240
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:06,560
I just wish I could have said thank you.

241
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:11,860
He'd be greatly honored by that princess.

242
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:24,100
Captain Smoker, Ms.

243
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:26,612
Hina, Sergeant Major Tashigi has arrived.

244
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:29,537
Welcome back, Sergeant Major!

245
00:15:29,620 --> 00:15:31,780
It sure has been a while, Tashigi.

246
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,270
Nina?

247
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,540
Glad to see you again.

248
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:39,320
If you'll excuse me.

249
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:42,718
I'm a little tired, so I'm
going to go get some rest.

250
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:47,340
We're back, Captain Smoker.

251
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,600
Did you get my report? Sure did.

252
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:51,075
Thanks for your work.

253
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:54,464
I heard about what happened
with the Straw Hats.

254
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:55,960
I'm sorry, sir.

255
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:58,037
I helped the pirates.

256
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:02,061
We also had an opportunity to
capture them, and I let it slip away.

257
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:04,340
It's all my fault.

258
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:07,080
My actions were shameful. I'm sorry.

259
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:10,577
